My database is designed to track consumer electronic devices and the companies that manufacture
them. It includes the category each device belongs to, and the operating system each device
runs. The goal of this databse is to be able to compare products, track release history, organize devices 
by manufacturer, category, OS, etc.

With this database, I am able to:
- Look up all devices made by a specific manufacturer
- Find all devices in a given category within a certain price range
- See which devices run a particular operating system or version
- Compare specific storage/color variants of a device, including their individual pricing 


Entities and Descriptions

Entity Type: Manufacturer
Sample instances: Apple, Samsung
Attributes: manufacturerID, companyName, Country, yearFounded

Entity Type: Device
Sample instances: iPhone 17, Galaxy S24
Attributes: deviceID, modelName, releaseYear, basePrice

Entity Type: Category
Sample instances: Smartphone, Laptop
Attributes: CategoryID, categoryName, Description, avgPriceRange

Entity Type: Operating System
Sample instances: iOS 17, Android 14
Attributes: odID, osName, versionNumber, Developer

Entity Type: Device Variant (NEW weak entity)
Sample instances: iPhone 17 - 256GB. Black, Galaxy S24 - 512GB, Silver
Attributes: variantNumber, Color, storageCapactiy, variantPrice

Relationships
- A Manufacturer produces one or more Devices (one to many)
- A device belongs to one Category (many to one)
- A Device runs one Operating System (many to many)
- A Device has one or more Device Variants (one to none - NEW)

Use Cases:
1. I want to look up all devices made by a specific manufacturer
2. I want to find all devices in a certain category within a certain price range
3. I want to see which devices run a particular operating system or version
4. I want to compare specific storage/color variants of a device, including their pricing (NEW) 
